# Illustration rules

These are illustrated picture books. Pictures do part of the storytelling.

- Do not generate a full illustration pass until the manuscript is locked and quality gates have passed or a documented override exists.
- Each spread needs art direction: purpose, cast, state, action, emotion, camera, props, continuity, text-safe area, must-include, must-not-include.
- Images should add information, humour, or emotion that the text does not already say.
- Leave reread details. Do not overload the frame.
- Visual consistency is a system, not a prompt slogan. Pass canonical references, wardrobe, temporary state, previous-spread reference, and art direction.
- Maintain `art/visual-state.yaml` during the book. It expires at the end unless promoted into canon.
- Character identity, age, relative height, hair, clothing colours, and distinctive features are non-negotiable once defined.
- Do not introduce extra named characters in the background.
- No frightening or boundary-breaking imagery beyond `bible/fear-and-content-boundaries.md`.
- Failed Visual QA images are eligible for automatic regeneration.
- Do not hard-code an image vendor. Use `tools/image-generation/`.
- Approved images only move to `art/approved/` after Visual QA pass or a documented exception.
